  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 815-10-35, time value equals the option premium minus intrinsic value. Here, intrinsic value is $45 minus $40 = $5, so time value is $8 minus $5 = $3. Time value reflects the probability the option will gain additional value before expiration, influenced by volatility and time remaining.
Wrong (A): Strike price minus stock price would yield a negative number for an in-the-money call and does not represent time value.
Wrong (B): The notional amount is the total contract value (shares times stock price), not a component of the time value calculation.
