-- Q3208: Derivatives and Hedging [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-10-35, when a derivative is not designated as a hedging instrument, all changes in its fair value are recognized in current period earnings. This creates earnings volatility because there is no corresponding hedged-item offset.
Wrong (A): Deferral in OCI applies only to the effective portion of derivatives designated as cash flow hedges under ASC 815-30. Undesignated derivatives do not receive OCI treatment.
Wrong (C): Derivatives cannot be ignored for accounting purposes. ASC 815 requires all derivatives to be recognized on the balance sheet at fair value with changes flowing through earnings or OCI.
Wrong (D): Adjusting the hedged item is a fair value hedge mechanism under ASC 815-25. Without hedge designation, no hedged-item adjustment is made.$EXPL$
