Wrong (A): Exchanging fixed and floating payments in the same currency describes a plain-vanilla interest rate swap, not a currency swap.
Wrong (B): Buying and selling the same currency simultaneously does not describe a swap. Currency swaps involve two different currencies over the contract term.
