UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-10-15, a derivative has three defining characteristics: (1) one or more underlyings and a notional amount or payment provision, (2) requires no initial net investment or one smaller than needed for a similar market response, and (3) its terms require or permit net settlement.
Wrong (A): Exchange trading is not required. Many derivatives such as OTC swaps and forwards are not exchange-traded but still qualify as derivatives under ASC 815.
Wrong (C): There is no maturity limitation. Derivatives can have contractual terms of any duration, including multi-year interest rate swaps and long-dated options.
