  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraphs 18-22, governments must capitalize infrastructure assets on the government-wide statement of net position. They can depreciate these assets normally or use the modified approach, which requires maintaining the asset at an established condition level and reporting preservation costs instead of depreciation.
Wrong (A): Infrastructure assets are not expensed when constructed. GASB requires capitalization of these long-lived assets on the government-wide statements.
Wrong (B): Infrastructure assets are not excluded from the balance sheet. They are reported as capital assets on the government-wide statement of net position.
