-- Q3231: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 67, an enterprise fund is required when the activity is financed by debt backed solely by fees and charges, when laws require cost recovery through fees, or when pricing policy establishes fees intended to recover costs including capital costs. Water utilities are a common example.
Wrong (A): Providing goods or services to internal departments describes an internal service fund, not an enterprise fund. Enterprise funds serve external users.
Wrong (B): Administering a defined benefit pension plan is reported in a fiduciary fund (pension trust fund), not an enterprise fund.
