-- Q3233: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 34, in Scenario A (bond-financed), the city records a $5M capital asset and $5M liability. Net investment in capital assets equals $5M minus $5M related debt, or $0, and unrestricted net position is unchanged because no existing resources were consumed. In Scenario B (cash-funded), net investment in capital assets is $5M and unrestricted decreases by $5M. Total net position is identical because the financing method only shifts amounts between components.
Wrong (B): In Scenario A, net investment in capital assets is $0 (not $5M) because the related debt must be subtracted. Cash-funded assets are capitalized under GAAP.
Wrong (C): The financing source does affect the component allocation. Bond financing creates a liability that reduces the net investment in capital assets component.
Wrong (D): Total net position is the same in both scenarios, not lower in Scenario A. The bond creates equal offsetting asset and liability entries.$EXPL$
