-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 14, government-wide financial statements present two primary columns: governmental activities (financed mainly by taxes and grants) and business-type activities (financed by fees charged to external users). Discrete component units appear in a separate column.
Wrong (A): Capital and operating is not the column structure for government-wide statements. This distinction applies to certain revenue and expenditure classifications within funds.
Wrong (B): Primary government and component units are reporting entity concepts but not the two main activity columns. Component units are shown separately from the primary government''s activities.
Wrong (C): General fund and special revenue fund are individual governmental fund types reported in fund-level statements, not columns in the government-wide statements.$EXPL$
