-- Q3235: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 14, paragraph 13, a legally separate entity is a component unit when the primary government is financially accountable, meaning it appoints a voting majority of the governing body and can either impose its will or a financial benefit/burden relationship exists. Such units are generally presented discretely in the government-wide statements.
Wrong (A): Financial interrelation alone without governance authority does not establish the component unit relationship. The primary government must appoint a voting majority to establish financial accountability.
Wrong (B): When operations are indistinguishable from the primary government, blending (not discrete presentation) is required. Discrete presentation keeps the component unit in a separate column.
Wrong (D): A federal agency providing funding is not a component unit of the receiving government. Component units are legally separate entities over which the primary government has financial accountability.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3235;
